  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xDBEC" flags="0x0">
    <title>VVEL Duration Target - Hot Intake Idle</title>
    <description>Exact 1ND3B. Address 0xE748; 8 rows x 8 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Mode 12 duration surface of the VVEL selector: hot-intake idle with the high-detonation state clear. The 1ND resolver stores the surface value directly; there is no floor lookup. Stock values are 1000 = 50.0 at every cell. Exact 1ND3B target-native table at 0xe748 bound to accessor 0x5f468 through literal 0x5f7a0, accessor 0x70514 through literal 0x7129c. Read by the resolver FUN_0005F468 at callsite 0x5F664 through the 8x8 uint16 wrapper 0x28674 with two byte coordinates: r7 is the byte 0xFFFE8073 (coolant temperature latch, DID 0x1101) and the stack slot is the byte 0xFFFE9796 (intake air temperature latch, DID 0x1106), both degC + 50. FUN_00070514 reads the surface at 0x7106A and 0x71132 with the same axes. JK78C indexes its surface 0x0000E1CE by engine speed and torque instead. 1ND3B shares the 1ND0A code layout and its stock bytes at this address.</description>
