  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x7A48" flags="0x0">
    <title>VVEL Duration Target - Mode 14</title>
    <description>Exact 1ND3B. Address 0xE6C8; 8 rows x 8 columns; uint16; map confidence code. Mode 14 duration surface of the VVEL selector, interpolated with the coordinates and axes of the hot-intake idle surfaces. Stock values are 960 = 48.0 at every cell. The 1ND0A machine FUN_0005D974 selects mode 14 on the hot-intake idle request when the knock-state byte 0xFFFEF5B3 (0xFFFE9488.bit6) or the snapshot byte 0xFFFEF4B6 (0xFFFE94CC.bit5) is set and either 0xFFFEF4B6 is set or the flag 0xFFFEF4CB is set; FUN_0005D0FC sets 0xFFFEF4CB when the idle target byte 0xFFFE92E9 (DID 0x110D, 12.5 RPM per count) reaches ROM8[0x87FD] = 52 and clears it below 52 - ROM8[0x8607] = 48. With the flag clear the same request selects mode 13, and with both bytes clear mode 12. FUN_00062DCC is the only writer of 0xFFFE94CC.bit5, a low-engine-speed flag: it sets while the sticky flag 0xFFFEB85A.bit1 is set and the RPM/12.5 latch 0xFFFE81AC is at or below the curve 0x13FC2 (52 = 650 RPM at every node) over the engine-oil-temperature latch 0xFFFE80F9 (DID 0x111F source 0xFFFE8179), or while that latch reaches ROM8[0x8774] = 255 with RPM/12.5 at or below ROM8[0x8772] = 44. The same function sets 0xFFFEB85A.bit1 from 0xFFFE94AE.bit1 and no code clears it; FUN_001110DA sets 0xFFFE94AE.bit1 once 0xFFFE94AE.bit0 and 0xFFFE94CC.bit4 have held until the counter 0xFFFE958F, reloaded from ROM8[0x8C63] = 10, reaches zero. FUN_001110DA belongs to the intake valve timing module, whose per-bank producer FUN_0010EA78 publishes DID 0x1138 and 0x1139 (INT/V SOL B1 and B2 in two public parameter lists) from the words 0xFFFE9694 and 0xFFFE9696 and writes the deviation words 0xFFFE9462 and 0xFFFE9464 around 0x8000. It sets 0xFFFE94AE.bit0 on the pass where the sequence flag 0xFFFEB89C.bit2 of FUN_00110222 falls, or where its own window flag 0xFFFE94B0.bit4 falls with that flag clear, while the gate 0xFFFEB7F3.bit4 is clear, the filter-seeded flag 0xFFFE94C4.bit7 is set, the hold counter 0xFFFE9571 is zero, and the stability flag 0xFFFE94CC.bit4 is set; it clears the bit whenever 0xFFFE94CC.bit4 is clear. The stability flag requires 0xFFFE948D.bit6, the word 0xFFFE9328 at or above 0x8000 + ROM8[0x8C2E] - 0x80 = 0x8006, and a filtered deviation word (0xFFFE8B2E, 0xFFFE8B30) within ROM8[0x8C5A] = 14 of its reference (0xFFFE8CA2, 0xFFFE8CA4) on at least one bank. The window opens with the stability flag and 0xFFFE947A.bit6 set, the delay counter 0xFFFE958E at zero, and bits 0 and 1 of 0xFFFEA9EA and 0xFFFEA9EC clear, and runs for the curve 0x146D6 over the engine-oil-temperature axis 0x1372C, 5 at every node. The gate seeds the filter and loads the hold counter from the curve 0x1451E over the axis 0x13618, 30 at every node of this image over 50 through 190. JK78C writes no value 14 to its mode byte. Exact 1ND3B target-native table at 0xe6c8 bound to accessor 0x5f468 through literal 0x5f7ac. Read by the resolver FUN_0005F468 at callsite 0x5F6AC through the 8x8 uint16 wrapper 0x28674 and stored at the mode 14 pair slot. The 1ND0A mode byte is 0xFFFEF4D0, published to 0xFFFE992C and 0xFFFEF5D0. JK78C stores the constant 50.0 for this mode and carries no table. 1ND3B shares the 1ND0A code layout and its stock bytes at this address.</description>
