  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xEBF5" flags="0x0">
    <title>Ignition Timing Surface - Cold State</title>
    <description>Exact 1ND3B. Address 0x9880; 16 rows x 16 columns; uint8; map confidence candidate. Cold timing-state surface. Selector 0004e1c0 uses it for both the active sample ffff160f and high-octane reference sample ffff1610 below coolant raw 107, then blends it into both samples through raw 131. The low seven bits feed timing state; bit 7 independently enables a knock-state path. This view edits mask 0x7F and preserves the other bits in each cell. The table is homologous to EV18A 0x9976 with a constant layout offset of +0x5c across the trio. Finisher 000267cc interpolates only bits 0..6 and copies bit 7 from the lower-left selected cell. The low-seven field is a crank-degree adjustment added to the computed base angle ffff23f1, not a direct absolute spark angle. The unit closure is the arithmetic chain to the J1979 PID 0x0E coordinate: ffff23bd=max(low7-ffff11af,0) at 0004af84; ffff1830=clamp_s8(ffff23f1+ffff23bd-ffff23c5-ffff12dc-ffff15ea-128+ffff1a7d+ffff134a) at 0004bee2, where ffff1a7d is centered at 64 so the map field enters as low7-64 beside base angle ffff23f1; ffff2404=ffff1830 at 0004c17a; scheduler 00020dfe copies ffff2404 to snapshot ffff2378 at 00021314..00021318; ffff12d6=clamp_s8(ffff2378+ffff11d6+ffff2356-ffff1ff6) at 0004db8c; ffff11da=clamp(ffff12d6+gated ffff564c,-7,50) at 0004dcf6; the rate-limited and bounded result is ffff11d4 at 0004df64, which PID 0x0E publishes as A/2-64 degBTDC. Every coefficient is 1, so one raw count is one crank degree while the field stays above threshold ffff11af, and raw 64 is the zero adjustment. The physical spark angle remains a hardware item. Definition address projected from JK08A 0000991a through JK08A-1ND.definition-addresses.csv: target ignition coordinator references this surface on every unselected cold-state path.</description>
