    <description>Exact 1ND3B. Address 0x14104; 1 rows x 16 columns; uint8; map confidence candidate. Coolant-indexed rising-edge DFCO entry RPM threshold in FUN 0004fbe2. The stock path selects it when current upstream mode ffff2458.bit5 is set and previous snapshot ffff245a.bit5 is clear; coarse vehicle speed ffff110e must be at least ROM8[000085fa]=4. Common-definition Map 1 uses the canonical stock storage. The comparison is strict RPM/25 &gt; threshold. Exact JK08A code interpolates both cut tables on every evaluation and selects this one for the rising mode edge. Target-vehicle A/B evidence in patches/hardware-results.toml shows that retaining this stock entry threshold does not force DFCO entry when the restore classifier returns a nonzero class. Result disposition: inline_comparison. Definition address projected from JK08A 00012718 through JK08A-1ND.definition-addresses.csv: homologous DFCO coordinator preserves the rising-edge table role and near-exact calibration shape. Static diagnostic context: Engine Coolant Temperature [code, homologous_community, via map evidence: indexed_by].</description>
