  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x4C33" flags="0x0">
    <title>Map 4 - Fuel Compensation - Main - Alternate</title>
    <description>Exact 1ND3B. Address 0x132F00; 16 rows x 16 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Alternate multiplicative fuel correction with raw 128 = 100% as neutral. It shares the index byte, both axes, and the interpolator of the projected default surface, and the downstream state selector reads it in place of that surface. Common-definition Map 4 storage is projected from 0xA2C0. Stock firmware does not reference this allocated storage; it becomes runtime-active only with the project map-switching patch. Exact 1ND3B target-native table at 0xa2c0 bound to accessor 0x30810 through literal 0x31164, accessor 0x44f1c through literal 0x454f8. The two 16x16 surfaces are read with the same index byte, the same axis pair, and the same interpolator in both accessors, so neither surface carries an engine-bank identity. The accessors publish four parallel compensation channels and the consumer selects one by a state code, then crossfades the value of the current state with the value of the previous state by a normalized progress weight where 0x8000 is 1.0. The default arm of that selector reads the projected canonical surface; this table is the arm the state code selects instead.</description>
